Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: support AN7563 native bridge offload

Manage the AN7563 SRAM flow table from the host and use its native bridge
key and action formats. Preserve ingress port, MAC, VLAN and IP-family
identity, validate the triggering packet before binding and retain the
packet DS field. Unsupported or ambiguous keys remain in software.

Track hardware-slot ownership and station/device references so teardown
cannot leave stale destinations or erase a replacement flow. Source-NPU
station tags provide separate Wi-Fi ingress domains and are stripped on
forwarding or restored on a CPU miss.

Do not advertise routed offload, per-flow counters or hardware HTB/ETS
scheduling on this implementation.

---
